        "original_id": "b2e70947-b511-5da5-8786-e7fb82b067d1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ruthe Blalock Jones\n- Organizations: Delaware Tribe of Indians, Delaware Nation, Stockbridge-Munsee Community\n- Roles: painter, printmaker\n- Places: Oklahoma, Bartlesville, Anadarko, Wisconsin\n- Topics: federally recognized tribes of Delaware Indians\n\nFacts:\n- Ruthe Blalock Jones was born in 1939.\n- Ruthe Blalock Jones is a Delaware-Shawnee-Peoria painter and printmaker from Oklahoma.\n- The Delaware Tribe of Indians is sometimes called the Eastern Delaware.\n- The Delaware Tribe of Indians is based in Bartlesville, Oklahoma.\n- The Delaware Tribe of Indians is one of three federally recognized tribes of Delaware Indians in the United States.\n- The other two federally recognized tribes of Delaware Indians are the Delaware Nation in Anadarko, Oklahoma, and the Stockbridge-Munsee Community of Wisconsin.",
